1
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:43,040
Thank you.

2
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,760
Thank you.

3
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:41,377
Pesci, what the hell
are you doing? Help me!

4
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:44,360
Stop this train right now, Pesci!

5
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,597
No way!

6
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:52,020
You have to stop this train!

7
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:58,617
Big bro but I don't know
the first thing about

8
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:02,137
stopping trains in a
matter of moments you and

9
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:04,477
Your power will be but a memory after that

10
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,580
I'll save my team and
I'll keep protecting Trish

11
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:09,930
Bucurati!

12
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:11,040
Damn you!

13
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:13,740
Big bro!

14
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:19,270
What?

15
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,400
I won't let this prick
take you away from me!

16
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:27,670
Nice!

17
00:02:27,753 --> 00:02:29,600
That was marvelous work, Pass.

18
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:32,540
Your quick-fire thinking
prevented a nasty end.

19
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:34,157
Talk about a close one!

20
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:37,577
He was almost a goner, but I
snagged him at the last second,

21
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:39,277
and now that he's on my hook,

22
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,772
he's not going anywhere.

23
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:45,196
But it feels like I've got two bodies
dangling off the end of the line.

24
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,920
It must be Pucurati.

25
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,121
He didn't bite it when they fell.

26
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,177
You're a formidable adversary.

27
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:56,097
My life started to flash
before my eyes just then.

28
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:59,797
I know I said something to the
effect of you being a lousy Cape,

29
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:01,468
but I take it all back now.

30
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,860
That was said in poor taste.

31
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:07,840
I see now you make decisions
with a fair and impartial eye.

32
00:03:08,260 --> 00:03:10,966
Your crew's lives are
as valuable as your own.

33
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,612
The more we duke it out,

34
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,717
the more apparent it is
the boss was right to

35
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:17,437
leave his estranged daughter
in your capable hands.

36
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,049
Yes, you've left quite
a strong impression.

37
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:25,160
However, Bucciarati, your
luck as a Cape just ran out!

38
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,560
You were so eager to leap
from this train before!

39
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:32,097
I hope you enjoy your ride
to the afterlife! Superman!

40
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:33,010
Superman!

41
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:34,960
Did you forget?

42
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:39,184
My aging powers are still thrusting
you into an early retirement!

43
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:41,080
Too slow!

44
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:43,660
It's funny.

45
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:48,528
Thanks to your younger brother's freaky
fishing line, my life has been spared.

46
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:50,410
What?

47
00:03:50,493 --> 00:03:52,517
He wasn't aiming for me in the least.

48
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,837
Could I be the unlucky one in all of this?

49
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:56,917
Just look at what happened with Mista.

50
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,097
It's a miracle he still has a pulse.

51
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:02,057
I unloaded three bullets
straight into his skull,

52
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:04,957
yet somehow the stronzo
is still drawing breath.

53
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,780
None of this makes any sense.

54
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:10,395
It's as if the sun suddenly
started rising in the west!

55
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,960
I told him everything he needs to know.

56
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,297
The energy from an attack
dealt on the fishing

57
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:18,145
line goes straight back
to the one on the hook!

58
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,080
It can't be!

59
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,460
Curse you, Bucciarati!

60
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:31,077
Whoa, my load just got
a hell of a lot lighter.

61
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:33,477
Looks like I lost that douche, Bucciarati.

62
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,880
We did it, Prosciutto!

63
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:36,611
We slaughtered that punk!

64
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,940
His age acceleration
is finally wearing off.

65
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:44,497
Now we just have to
finish off, loser hook.

66
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,410
Yeah.

67
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,240
What the heck?

68
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:54,237
I know for a fact that I
hooked Big Bro's right hand.

69
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:57,379
And I'm positive there was
nothing else on the line.

70
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:00,240
His pinky.

71
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:03,246
I'm sure it was on the
right side of the hook.

72
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:07,360
But it's different now.

73
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:11,340
The pinky's on the left side of the hook.

74
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:13,340
But how is that possible?

75
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,897
How'd I hook the left hand?

76
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:16,804
What the heck is going on here?

77
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,757
Something weird's happening out there.

78
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,097
Why is my Big Bro's left hand hooked now?

79
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:23,297
Would someone make this
weird shit make sense?

80
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,498
Because I'm freaking the F out here!

81
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:27,397
Although now that I think about it,

82
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,717
Big Bro did feel a teeny
bit heavier than normal.

83
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,624
Hey you, it's the fishing pole!

84
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,839
You gotta hit the emergency brakes!

85
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,017
This entire train has been infected!

86
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:40,860
All the aches and pains are gone, but
something still doesn't feel right. What?

87
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,300
This guy's all better!

88
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,537
Are you even listening to me?

89
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,957
Tell the driver to stop the
train before we all bite him!

90
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,097
This can't be real.

91
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:50,277
If all these people are
starting to get better,

92
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,897
then the body that dropped
from my line must have been...

93
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:53,917
Oh god, no!

94
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,880
There's no way it was him!

95
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,940
No, Big Bro, please no!

96
00:05:58,260 --> 00:05:59,560
Hey, I'm talking here!

97
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:02,157
Pay attention or we're
all gonna die, you idiot!

98
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,740
Big Bro Fusuto, say it as it's all!

99
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,118
What am I gonna do?

100
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:07,418
What am I gonna do?

101
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,020
What am I gonna do?

102
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:12,857
If he's not around, those guys
will come out of the turtle?

103
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,175
and that's it for me!

104
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,070
Achoo!

105
00:06:16,153 --> 00:06:17,117
I gotta think of something!

106
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:19,257
Why are you crying like a damn baby?

107
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:21,575
Make somebody stop the train, strunzo!

108
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:28,060
Get in Mamoni out of the way if
you won't do anything to help.

109
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,025
I'll just have to do it myself

110
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:36,840
What's going on?

111
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,700
The aging hasn't stopped after all

112
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:44,460
But your auntie you're not again.

113
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,700
No, don't tell me

114
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,190
What?

115
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,177
Finish this.

116
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:00,280
Hurry, big boy. Bro!

117
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,750
Bro!

118
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:09,460
You were right, big bro.

119
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:12,740
Just like always, you
were absolutely right.

120
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:15,077
Once you've caught your target,

121
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:18,257
your only priority is to hold
on to them no matter what.

122
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:20,737
You have to keep your stand activated even

123
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:23,137
if it means you end up
losing an arm or a leg.

124
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:24,880
Oh, Big Bro.

125
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:28,637
With the state he's in, he
won't survive much longer.

126
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,760
He's a goner.

127
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:33,777
It's just a matter of time
before he takes his last breath.

128
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:36,700
And still he refuses
to withdraw his stand.

129
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,645
A warrior till the bitter end.

130
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,917
In order to complete our mission,

131
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,057
we have to capture Trish
whatever the personal cost.

132
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:49,022
Right, Big Bro?

133
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:52,812
We've come too close to the
finish light to turn back now.

134
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,050
I get it.

135
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,300
I understand, prosciutto.

136
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,188
You taught me true bravery.

137
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,937
I don't just hear your words now.

138
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:05,300
I feel them in the depths of my heart.

139
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,860
It's just like you
always told me, big bro.

140
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:13,820
When the dark dot comes,
the deed is already done.

141
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,480
Well, what do you know about that?

142
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:27,840
Taking life doesn't feel half bad.

143
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,380
It wasn't nearly as scary as
I thought it was gonna be.

144
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:37,160
And with that, my days of
being called Mamoni are over.

145
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:41,546
From now on, I'll be the pitiless
pesci of death feared by all.

146
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,457
I'm gonna put an end to
you once and for all.

147
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:55,716
While my big bro's powers
still have a little potency.

148
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:59,697
Bucciarati, you gotta get that hook
out of you before he retaliates!

149
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:00,610
Yeah?

150
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:04,398
So, you unzipped your hand, did you?

151
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:06,690
What?

152
00:09:06,773 --> 00:09:10,157
Does this freak somehow have a way of
anticipating every move that I make?

153
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,480
I can read you like a picture book.

154
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:15,757
My hook's itching to get
inside and rip you apart,

155
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:18,958
and your wrist is too good
an entry point to pass up.

156
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:22,355
The hook's shooting up your
arm like a bat out of hell!

157
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,480
How'd it slip out again?

158
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,190
Merda!

159
00:09:34,273 --> 00:09:38,417
Every time I go to pull it out, he anticipates
all my movements to the centimeter.

160
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:39,940
This guy's pretty good.

161
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:44,037
You've lost your mind if you think
I'll let you get away from me now.

162
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:46,280
I'll never let Big Bro Spirit die.

163
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:49,977
I'll snatch up Trish and complete
the mission in his honor.

164
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:50,890
Vucerati!

165
00:09:50,973 --> 00:09:52,331
The dipshit's down there!

166
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:56,597
If we get rid of that guy, Churno and
the other guys will go back to normal.

167
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,974
After that, they can take down Po 'boy!

168
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:00,490
Understood.

169
00:10:00,573 --> 00:10:02,081
But that's easier said than done.

170
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:07,089
You're about to get a helping of the
torment and anguish my Big Bro suffered!

171
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:12,330
Luchirazi!

172
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:18,008
Asshole must have grabbed onto something,
which would mean that he's climbing!

173
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,817
You're heading right for the power lines!

174
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:24,820
Now get me!

175
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,460
What's going on here?

176
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:38,117
I felt something hit, but it didn't
feel like a body being bisected.

177
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,440
I feel the vibrations of a pulse.

178
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:43,036
Bucciarati is definitely still alive.

179
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:45,560
He got himself back inside the train.

180
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:49,280
You lucked out, Bucciarati.

181
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:53,697
The way things are shaking out, we'll have
to take down this bastard face to face.

182
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:54,610
You're right.

183
00:10:54,693 --> 00:10:57,220
But we don't have the
means. Not like this.

184
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,374
We've run out of time.

185
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:03,140
The hook is already burrowing
into my chest cavity. Oh, no!

186
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:07,357
My hook is 12 centimeters
away from your heart. Whoops.

187
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,460
Make that 11.

188
00:11:09,060 --> 00:11:10,880
I misjudged terribly.

189
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:13,846
The thug with the aging
powers was formidable,

190
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,920
but I see now he was
never our greatest threat.

191
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:21,760
The real terror on the train was
hidden behind that innocuous tool.

192
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:24,437
What are you planning
to do now, Bucciarati?

193
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:27,402
That hook will skewer your
heart before too long.

194
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,160
Nine away, eight away.

195
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,071
I suppose I'll have to teach him a lesson.

196
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:37,160
The only way to overcome his stand is to
make this Koglione understand something.

197
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,960
I have Determinazione in spades!

198
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:41,440
Do it, Zipperman!

199
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:45,920
What the hell are you doing?

200
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:55,550
Bucciarati!

201
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,070
Huh?

202
00:11:57,153 --> 00:11:58,000
He's gone!

203
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:00,240
Not even a hint of a pulse.

204
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,497
And I don't sense any breathing either.

205
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:03,700
But how?

206
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,660
I'm so confused.

207
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,276
How'd I completely lose track of him?

208
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,420
You're starting to worry me, Bucciarati.

209
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:15,860
I know we don't have a lot of
options, but this is too much.

210
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:17,707
Are you sure you'll be okay?

211
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,897
Quiet yourself, number six.

212
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:23,440
We must wait till he leaves.

213
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,297
Acts like this are what it means to have.

214
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,262
Determinazione.

215
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:29,980
Dammit, he's gone!

216
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:33,456
His stand lets him slip off
my hook whenever he wants!

217
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:35,120
He could be anywhere!

218
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,540
He could ambush me from any angle!

219
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,010
No!

220
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:41,497
I gotta pull it together!

221
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:43,815
Paranoia is a sign of mental weakness!

222
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:46,196
That's what Prosciutto would tell me!

223
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:48,480
Be confident, Pesci.

224
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:52,977
If anyone can find a hidden heartbeat
on this speeding death trap from hell,

225
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:54,200
it's you, brother.

226
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:55,840
Damn straight!

227
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:59,880
There's no way Bucciarati is
as mobile as he used to be.

228
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:04,671
I bet big money that cowardly bastardo
is hiding out somewhere near my hook!

229
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:08,760
The line!

230
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,864
He's making it even longer now!

231
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:14,022
You've got to put yourself
back together and run!

232
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,400
I can't do that.

233
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,500
He still can't tell where I am.

234
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:24,480
And it'll stay that way as long
as I remain perfectly still.

235
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:27,820
Right now, I have to stay motionless.

236
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,320
That proves my resolve.

237
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:33,277
Listen for the blood
coursing through his veins.

238
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:35,654
Find his beating heart and destroy him.

239
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,040
Gotta catch.

240
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:41,797
But it's not the one I wanted.

241
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:43,233
The weight's all wrong.

242
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,500
It's a tourist!

243
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,317
It's fate, but there's no question.

244
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,300
It's a heart.

245
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:55,450
Not good!

246
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:57,366
He's zeroed in on your heart!

247
00:13:58,620 --> 00:13:59,450
Muncherati!

248
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:02,386
You said all you were
gonna do was stay still,

249
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:05,598
not cleave your heart in
half to stop the vibrations!

250
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,540
Has he lost his mind?

251
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:12,174
No one can live for very long if their
heart and lungs don't work, right?

252
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:20,260
Dammit! Nothing!

253
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:23,500
This place is silent
as a freaking cemetery!

254
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:28,656
Slippery Katsone must have snuck off
somewhere with that zipper of his!

255
00:14:35,860 --> 00:14:37,880
You've taken this too far!

256
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,180
What the hell?

257
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,341
Where is this bastard hiding now?

258
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:45,510
Huh?

259
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:50,020
Wait, what if that Gazzone Bucciarati
really finished off prosciutto?

260
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:54,875
If my bro's stand is gone, then the
guys in the turtle will be after me!

261
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,060
Damn it all!

262
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,120
Screw this noise!

263
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,520
You messed with the wrong guy!

264
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:04,540
We did it!

265
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:06,177
Poor idiot gave up and left!

266
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:10,142
That determinazione of yours totally
threw the Devi off the trail.

267
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,697
You sure as hell showed
that guy who's boss.

268
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:15,077
Now hurry up and zip
your body back together.

269
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:16,660
Come on, get a move on.

270
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,520
How strange life is.

271
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:32,640
What bad luck.

272
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,084
Just hang in there, Bucciarati.

273
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:39,745
Controlling bullets is
the most I'm able to do.

274
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:43,440
His drive got me totally off guard.

275
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:46,660
So, he's the victor.

276
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:50,090
Dammit!

277
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,709
Why won't this train stop?

278
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:54,910
Huh?

279
00:15:54,993 --> 00:15:55,940
What's happening?

280
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:13,660
Becbrough, I'm coming!

281
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,720
That was a train ride from hell.

282
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:23,565
One that I would not have survived
without some luck on my side.

283
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:28,478
But I'm happy to say the
journey led me right to you.

284
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:36,420
You'll suffer for what
you've done, Bucciarati.

285
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,140
We got him!

286
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:40,360
Hell yeah for determinazione!

287
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:44,237
The last thing my big bro sees before he

288
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:46,577
dies will be your corpse
thrown into the wind.

289
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:47,490
Got it?

290
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,380
What the hell?

291
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:56,060
Consider me impressed.

292
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:58,017
You've got some sharp peepers.

293
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,517
That expression.

294
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,894
His eyes look like they've
witnessed years of bloodshed.

295
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:05,560
His composure is downright menacing.

296
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:08,751
Simple tricks aren't going to work on him.

297
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:10,410
Do it.

298
00:17:10,493 --> 00:17:12,160
Glory is yours for the taking.

299
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:14,520
Finish him off, Pesci.

300
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:20,460
My time has come, but I'll be
watching you from the next life.

301
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:21,960
Make me proud.

302
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:29,880
I'll avenge my bro with your death!

303
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:33,690
What?

304
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,620
That's such a predictable move.

305
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:41,110
Ugh!

306
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:45,597
Shooting straight up the arm to the
cardiac muscle was always my Code.

307
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:49,974
Of course, that was when I didn't have
the balls to try anything riskier.

308
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:53,217
But now my finisher is an assault
straight to the heart of my prey.

309
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:57,857
Nothing will stop me from steamrolling
your brother-killing ass into extinction!

310
00:17:57,940 --> 00:18:01,352
I'll rip your heart out and
tear it into a million pieces!

311
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:19,700
You should save the victory speech
until after you've won the fight.

312
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:22,580
That's how a true mafiosi does it.

313
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:27,580
Did I lose?

314
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:31,240
Is this really how I bite the big one?

315
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:32,720
No way.

316
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:36,380
Not before I play my ultimate hand.

317
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:38,980
Go ahead.

318
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:42,640
Take her and run. Wait now.

319
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:44,840
And I'll let her keep her life.

320
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:47,860
Look, he's got the turtle! What? Where?

321
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:49,600
I'm not gonna make it.

322
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:53,637
But before I go, the least I can do
is give you a little parting gift.

323
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:56,580
The gift of knowing
you failed your Family.

324
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:00,777
Now watch as I crush this
thing into turtle soup!

325
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:03,197
The rest of the group is
gonna be smashed to death!

326
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:06,200
You know, I admired
that glint in your eyes.

327
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:08,637
There was an unrelenting nobility to them.

328
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:10,485
You don't see that very often.

329
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,480
Pity, it's vanished.

330
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:15,260
Now you're nothing but a disgraced swine.

331
00:19:15,820 --> 00:19:16,650
Am I now?

332
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,030
I disagree.

333
00:19:18,113 --> 00:19:22,360
The only ones falling for grace are
your friends and this damn turtle!

334
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:23,960
It's over.

335
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:26,660
Enjoy burning in hell, Bucerati!

336
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:35,598
I can tell you've lived life
as the eternal screw-up.

337
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,308
Don't change on my account.

338
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:54,400
ARRIVA Trish

339
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:28,477
It's fairly obvious we can't
travel by train from here on out.

340
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,017
Yeah, I think you're right.

341
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:32,857
There's no telling what they know
and who they've told about us.

342
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:37,617
I'm sure they've figured out where we're
going by now, and what the Turtle can do.

343
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:41,171
We'll have to use another form
of transportation from here.

344
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:45,217
There's something I'd like to ask you.

345
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:47,300
Would you be willing to cooperate?

346
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:51,647
Apologies, but we don't have
authorization to do such a thing.

347
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:54,839
You know our mission is
only to safeguard your life.

348
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,960
You will answer my questions.

349
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:59,680
Tell me, just who am I really?

350
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,274
What the hell is this?

351
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:03,357
How did it get on the ground?

352
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:04,400
I want answers.

353
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:07,680
Why are these bizarre marks
appearing near my feet?

354
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:12,540
How did a father I've never even
met turn me into a walking target?

355
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:17,040
As I thought, the boss's
daughter is a stand user.

356
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,040
Well, answer me!

357
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:29,040
It's currently 6.34 p .m.

358
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:32,892
I arrived at the scene 20
minutes after the train stopped.

359
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:36,300
Prosciutto is dead next to the tracks.

360
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:38,351
Pesci has been mutilated.

361
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:41,009
The pieces are scattered
near the riverbed.

362
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:45,877
Judging from the bloodbath here, this must
be the work of Bucciaranti's Zipperman.

363
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,560
And what about his team and the girl?

364
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:49,760
Long gone.

365
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:53,300
Can you track him, Melone? Yes.

366
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:58,209
Those two disfigured losers actually
managed to do something useful for once.

367
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:02,480
I've got a decent blood sample now.

368
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,520
From Bucciarati.

369
00:22:16,660 --> 00:22:19,697
I can't get you out of my mind.

370
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:23,217
Since you'll be all I see!

371
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:26,257
I would give anything.

372
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:30,317
Just to make you understand me!

373
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:34,657
I don't give a damn about nothing else.

374
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:38,217
Freaking you is all I need!

375
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:41,057
I need your body.

376
00:22:41,140 --> 00:22:42,900
I need your body.

377
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:10,700
Tell me.

378
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:14,480
What must I do?

379
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:16,680
To show how much

380
00:23:17,780 --> 00:23:20,577
I'm a freak in you?

381
00:23:20,660 --> 00:23:27,080
What must I do?

382
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:29,777
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

383
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:34,960
To show how much I'm a freak in you?

384
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:43,840
Thank you.

385
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:13,730
You
